WEBVTT

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.880
Locking procedure complete.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.080
Stabilization of regolith, all green.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.090
Installing the base pipe into mesh 5687.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.970
Rotational orbit within Yarkovsky
effect influence predictions.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.960
Maintaining values suitable
for excavation work.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.080
Safety standards for excavation under microgravity fulfilled.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.480
Well then, commence trial digging.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.300
Maintaining current drill pipe rotation.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.320
Magnetic solid, all green.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.480
Surrounding environment
change within standards.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.540
Internal porosity approximately 40%.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.160
Within expected range.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.240
Professor.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:07.570
Would be nice if we finally hit
a vein now, wouldn't it?

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.080
In terms of budget, this is our last dig.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:14.160
Let's put our hope in Maya's geological predictions.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:18.760
If it's that way, wouldn't it have been more
reasonable to pick Delta 9 as the site?

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.580
Delta 9 is enveloped in a level 4
Miguel Storm right now.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:26.420
I can't put you in such danger, right?

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.930
But according to the observation data...

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:30.080
There is something on the sensors.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:31.820
Orange alert.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.400
Drill pipe, emergency stop.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.540
Did we hit bedrock?

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.240
Yes.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:39.440
Let's head out there in I-machines
and verify the platform's condition.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:40.610
Affirmative.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:41.690
Maya.

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:43.690
Huh? Am I going as well?

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:44.900
Obviously.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:49.410
It might be your first dig,
but you're still a member of this team.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:56.860
But I'm specializing in geological surveys,
work on the site is a bit...

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.880
You have a second-level MT license, right?

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.140
It's just 200 hours of training and simulation.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.770
What's your average synchronization ratio?

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.460
It's just 86.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.700
But that's exceptional!

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.690
But......

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:09.420
Don't worry, Maya.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.880
It's just an I-machine.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.480
You'll revive even if you die.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.580
MT system booting up.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:19.330
After your thought data is backed up,
you will be transferred to the I-machine.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.440
Back-up complete.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.040
Transferring.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.090
Eh, uh, this...

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:28.540
How is the synchronization?

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:29.980
Well, on numbers...

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.700
I think it's okay?

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.330
Set your sensory data to the height
of 18 meters, optimal settings.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:37.660
After that, just get used to it.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.340
Let's go, Maya.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.400
Y-yes.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.020
Maya, hurry up.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:51.960
Um, to be honest, I am really scared right now.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.300
You alright with the scholarship being revoked?

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:57.380
I'm going! I'm going!

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:00.810
ID number confirmed.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.090
Mikuri Maya.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.020
Looks like we found our target.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.900
Hey hey, are we up against
amateurs like those?

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.290
It doesn't matter.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.920
We're just doing our respective jobs.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.700
Lifting the drill pipe up until the safety limits.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.440
As I thought, metal deposits.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:57.250
Was it an agglomeration of mineral
and metal asteroids then?

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.180
Maya, why couldn't you predict this?

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:03.380
I thought we would be digging at Delta 9,

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:07.170
so I didn't have time for a geophysical
exploration of Omega 3.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.580
I'm sorry.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:09.540
Hmm...

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:15.600
There's no other way to continue drilling other than
breaking apart the metal with a directional blasting.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.360
Maya, back me up.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:18.130
Roger.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:22.220
Synchronizing vision data with the sensors
on the bottom hole assembly.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:25.840
Maya, where's the point we can
break with minimal influence?

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:30.500
Going off the current excavation
data, it should be here.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.440
Well done.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:35.100
It aligns with my predictions too.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:38.600
Let's perform directional blasting there then.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.580
Well, did it break apart?

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.210
Drill pipe resuming excavation, confirmed.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:50.200
Maya, collect the metal and perform
a chemical analysis of it.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.240
Okay.

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:54.140
Red alert!

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:56.290
Bottom hole assembly pressure rising!

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:59.720
Did we hit the Orichalt vein directly?

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:05.450
Professor!

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:08.810
Maya!

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:19.580
Mind reload.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.880
We lost the I-machines, huh.

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:23.660
Well, there's nothing we could've done.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:26.000
We got right into a Miguel Storm, after all.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.140
Let's evacuate the ship out of here,

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:31.610
or it will get sucked into a Miguel Storm as well.

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:32.380
Huh?

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.640
Can we?

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:38.850
It looks like Maya's consciousness
data is still in the I-machine.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:39.980
Romanov.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:45.010
According to the space law, ensuring the safety
of a ship is the number one priority.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:45.780
I see.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:49.180
Professor, please don't leave me out here.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.660
Of course.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.200
You have a good head on
your shoulders, after all.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.130
Professor!

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:55.900
Romanov!

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:56.740
Where are you?

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:58.800
Save me please!

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.290
Somebody save me!

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:03.240
Right arm!

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:04.440
My right arm!

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:06.970
This is bad!

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:09.220
Someone, someone!

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:17.440
It hurts!

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:21.800
Cut off the pain sense in your right arm!

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.560
The pain data in your right arm.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:29.420
Thank you very much.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:30.360
No need to.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:32.440
Besides, I have to apologize here.

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:33.940
He's so rough.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:35.940
I'm sorry, but you are?

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.220
Excavators.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.520
Oh, an excavation company then.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.840
Hey Pops, the student's alright here.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:45.940
How's it on your end?

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:52.410
So they abandoned their excavation site.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:55.890
Which means we can do as we please with it.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.100
Let's go get it!

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.080
All of the Orichalt over there!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.360
Grayman, what's the storm level?

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:03.700
Level 3.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:07.880
It's a place where the academy was digging,
I've got great expectations for it!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.860
Excuse me, what are you going to do?

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:13.040
Help ourselves to that Orichalt
ore instead of you.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.680
Rick, we're within range.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:23.620
Gotcha.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:26.740
Give us a great cut, Id!

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:28.940
Just breaking in like that?

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:29.960
This is crazy!

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.330
It's fine.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.880
We're using the hole you made.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:42.380
Ore located.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:44.060
Returning with a Miguel Jump.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:44.930
Alright.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:46.520
Ready when you are.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.180
Whoa!...

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.250
A Miguel Jump in a place like this...

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:01.210
Huh?

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:02.720
Is that all of the treasure?

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:06.010
Hey, hey, is the academy's eye that bad?

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:11.220
I'm sorry, but we were supposed
to dig that piece of Orichalt ore.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:13.160
Could you please return it?

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:16.360
The academy abandoned
the site and ran away.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:20.420
But if I don't bring results I'm going
to be unable to get scholarship!

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:22.300
And if I can't go to the academy...

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:23.760
You know, you should really
be running away.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:24.280
Eh?

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:25.640
The Storm Burst is coming.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.090
Mikuri Maya.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:37.800
Your genetic signal data has been
assigned the number B3224.

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:42.490
You are admitted to the Federation Academy's
Cosmological Geology department.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.090
Thank you very much.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.660
And uh, what about support?

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:50.280
This course provides not just
learning environment,

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:53.940
you will be provided with lodging and
support at this academy as well.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.300
That's very helpful.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.700
I suppose this system is necessary for you,

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.090
having lost your parents at such a young age.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:03.700
But do you even like cosmological geology?

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:08.340
Well, in the first place it's because
of living and independence...

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.810
And the fact you get financial support.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:12.440
Well, I have to live on something after all...

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:15.650
So as long as you're alive, you're alright with
being swept along with whatever happens?

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.820
Well, how should I say it...

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:22.420
I mean, I ended up going to space anyway...

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.120
Well, the arrangements have
been made already.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.280
H-huh?

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.250
Oh, you're awake?

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:31.100
You saved me?

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.400
Thank you very much!

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:33.460
Don't worry about it.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.800
People have to help each other out.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.330
By the way, where is this?

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:38.650
Our headquarters, little lady.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:39.900
Headquarters?

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:40.680
Yes.

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:45.880
Our company's pride - Stulti, a ship
specialized for excavation work.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:48.570
It might look shabby, but it's great inside.

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:50.900
There's even a living area
for I-machines inside.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.490
For I-machines, huh...

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:56.220
Wait, I'm still in an I-machine!

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.360
This is bad, I'm going past allocated time!

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:01.930
I apologize, but first of all I need
to return to my own body!

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:07.840
Error?

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:11.370
Mind reload data sync not located?

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:12.600
My body?

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:14.910
What happened to my body?

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.250
Have you seen the research vessel?

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:28.370
The academy excavation and
research vessel I came on!

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.210
Sure did.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:31.010
It flew away somewhere.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:31.840
Eh?

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:35.820
They probably went back to
the Albireo relay station.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:37.860
No way...

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:40.800
Did they really return with
my body on board...

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:42.650
Put it in.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:43.400
Huh?

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:45.180
It's a spare right arm.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.080
Put it in.

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.220
Good thing you had a common body, eh.

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.780
You know how to switch joint modes, right?

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:53.660
Um, there's a lot I have to thank you for,

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:57.720
but would it be possible for you to
take me to the exploration vessel?

00:11:57.720 --> 00:11:58.620
Oh?

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:03.770
You don't sound very grateful for someone
who got her life saved, you know.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.660
Um, who might you be?

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.620
Captain of this Stulti here,

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:09.660
Grayman.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.340
And his daughter, Claire.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:14.140
Oh, my name is Mikuri Maya.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:17.610
Third year in the Cosmological Geology
of the Federation Academy.

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:19.480
Set the joint mode.

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:20.900
Oh, okay.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:24.740
How is it? Should work like normal.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:27.840
Thank you very much, this is a lifesaver.

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:28.700
Girlie.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:29.780
Y-Yes?

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:31.460
Getting back to our talk.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:36.600
Do you realize how much it will cost
to get you alone to the station?

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:37.740
Forget about it.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:38.920
Too bad.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:40.770
Well, that's life for you.

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.620
What are you saying?

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:45.600
If I lose my body, I'll die!

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:47.570
I'll pay you back for sure!

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:50.050
It's not an amount a student could pay.

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:53.200
I could pay in installments or credit...

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.560
Our captain is an impatient guy.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:56.960
No way...

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:03.260
However, depending on the conditions, I
might up listening to your request after all.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:06.340
Eh? Are you the captain from just now?

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:07.860
Why in an I-machine?

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:08.970
What's with you?

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.420
Listening to her request,
you must be in a good mood.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:16.810
Girlie, we're an excavation company
that specializes in Orichalt.

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:21.770
I've heard that you're excavators,
but specializing in Orichalt?

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:23.100
Yep, we are.

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:29.320
I'm sorry, what did you say?

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:31.770
Girlie, are you not used to I-machines?

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:32.840
Yes, I'm not.

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:34.900
Try setting the sound level to 5.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.540
Can you hear me?

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:41.920
Oh, I hear you!

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.240
It's fine now.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:44.290
That's a relief.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:47.740
You know, we're always short on hands, so...

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:55.160
So you see, if you work your travel expenses off,
we'll take you to the relay station or wherever.

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:56.620
Really?

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:57.840
For reals.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:59.280
Thank you very much!

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:00.120
I'll do my best!

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:03.250
Alright then, let's talk business.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:04.180
Okay.

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:07.420
This is the target for now.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:11.570
Outer edge body in the Albireo
double binary system, Delta 9.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:15.820
Length around 20 km, estimated Orichalt deposits are A-rank.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:18.960
Hey, hey, why's a place like
that still untouched?

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:21.160
There's got to be a catch, right?

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.120
That's right.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:26.730
Pretty much the entire surface of the
asteroid gets randomly enveloped

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:30.930
in a level 4 Miguel Storm at times, so no
excavation company laid hands on it yet.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.540
Well that's quite a pickle now!

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.650
Guess we can't do it without data.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:36.960
Umm...

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:38.410
What is it, girlie?

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:40.980
I know this asteroid.

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:42.090
Really?

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:44.260
It was an observation target
for one of my seminars.

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:48.660
Originally, we were supposed
to do a digging test there,

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:51.240
but the professor suddenly
changed the excavation site...

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:53.920
Well that's a lovely coincidence!

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:57.580
Maya, since you were planning
to dig there anyway,

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:01.330
do you happen to know of a way to reach
the surface of Delta 9, by any chance?

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.320
Um, is this alright?

00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:05.840
Sure, if you know of a way, tell us.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:06.940
Alright.

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:11.780
From 10 years' worth of spectrum
observation data I got...

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:14.120
Um, input access...

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:16.360
Permission to input movement data granted.

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:17.700
Thank you.

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:22.760
At this trajectory it should be mostly
safe from a Miguel Storm.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:25.810
I also found a spot where the
storm does not appear.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:26.520
Eh?

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:30.240
Using that spot, it should be relatively
easy to perform excavation.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:34.090
If you're telling the truth,
this job should be easy money...

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:36.290
Her data analysis isn't bad.

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:38.780
Making an attempt here is worth it.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.020
Well if Id says so, it's settled.

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:43.500
Wonderful, Maya!

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.420
For Id to recognize you!

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:49.370
If this excavation goes well, I think you'll
be able to get to the station right away.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.130
Eh?

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:51.200
Really?

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.060
I'll give it my all!

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:01.520
What is this vehicle?

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:02.560
Cool, isn't it?

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:05.010
It's custom-made by USP!

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:08.800
Hey, student.

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:10.800
It's Maya. Mikuri Maya.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:11.980
You're stupid, aren't you.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:13.120
Stupid?

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:13.740
Yeah.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.640
What do you mean by that?

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:21.520
If you would have used that analysis data as a bargaining chip, you could have easily gone to wherever you wanted.

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:22.370
Oh...

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:23.600
It's in sight.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:25.490
Delta 9.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:28.260
Now, we just need to get on the trajectory
the little lady provided us...

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:29.040
Wait, Rick.

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:29.770
Huh?

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:30.580
What's wrong?

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:33.660
Ugh, looks like there's somebody
there already.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:34.800
Can you see them?

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.010
From this distance?

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:40.210
A lady in this trade needs info, you see.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:43.210
Do you mean you've got illegal modifications?

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:44.970
Don't you worry about it!

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:48.440
Looks like it's the Fujima corporation.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:53.650
And what exactly is a major "safety first"-company
doing in a dangerous place like this?

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:55.980
Wait, look at their excavation point.

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:57.840
It's the same as we were planning to use.

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:02.130
In that case it means the Fujima corporation
has the same data as you, little lady.

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:03.420
No way!

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:06.560
The Delta 9 observation data was
only at the professor's seminar!

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.170
Then he must've sold it.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:09.300
That info.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:10.380
Sold?

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.370
Who?

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:15.980
You don't mean the professor?

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:19.700
Looks like he was able to properly turn that
knowledge into money, unlike you.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.340
Don't say it like that!

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:23.520
Huh? What are you?

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:27.700
An I-machine?

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:28.960
An unmanned guard robot.

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:29.980
Guard?

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.780
Protecting Delta 9.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:33.930
They've spotted us!

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:37.290
What, no warning?

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:38.770
Don't shoot!

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:39.920
We're civilians!

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:42.250
It's no use, they're shooting to take us down.

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:44.810
But why?

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:49.730
They don't want other people to know they're
digging using illegally obtained info.

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:55.170
In this line of work this happens all the time.

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:06.580
This is an act of aggression, isn't it?

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:08.260
This is against Federation law!

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:09.260
So is what they're doing!

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.530
Thank you very much!

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:23.080
If you've got damaged parts,
exchange them later.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.570
This isn't the problem here!

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:26.200
There sure is a lot of them!

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.720
Captain, you're up!

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:28.560
Gotcha!

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:32.880
If we let them slow us down too much,
they'll just make away with our treasure!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.290
Captain, prepare the rig.

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:37.080
Aren't you rushing a bit?

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:43.610
To the drilling team: some strange
company is approaching.

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:44.980
How is your progress?

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:48.690
No problems here, we
should hit the ore soon.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:52.290
Papa, the Fujima corporation
is trying to reach the vein!

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.340
Say what?!

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.480
Id, you were right.

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:56.500
We've got to hurry!

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:59.480
Papa, I've locked on the target point.

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:00.580
In that case, shoot it!

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:01.130
Got it.

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:05.000
They're insane!

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.480
A drilling rig is coming!

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:07.330
Run!

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:11.900
What are you doing?

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:15.080
If it takes such an impact, the Orichalt
will become unstable!

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:17.220
That's why we'll recover it before it does!

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:18.560
You'll die!

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:20.050
It's fine.

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:23.570
You've got to enjoy this moment, right now.

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:26.340
You can't just say something so detached!

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:33.020
Well that's a whole lot.

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:38.370
Guess there's no choice.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:47.100
To think it'd be this huge...

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:49.020
Id, you alive?

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:50.650
How do I look to you?

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.120
Just short of being dead, I guess?

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:54.240
Good observation.

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:06.770
So, does this happen every time?

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:08.260
Id is special.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.610
He loses himself when it comes
to collecting Orichalt.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:13.410
Says he doesn't know why himself.

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:14.960
He doesn't know?

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:16.250
And so, uh...

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:16.960
What?

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:21.900
Isn't what you all are doing
kind of like piracy?

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:23.940
What a cruel thing to say!

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:26.330
We're a wholesome excavation company!

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:28.480
Is that really so?

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:30.210
That's...

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:32.570
The Planet Federation's 7th Cosmic Fleet!

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:34.300
We're saved!

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.980
If we just get the military to protect us...

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:37.900
What are you talking about?
We're running away.

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:38.530
Eh?

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:40.780
Do you want to be caught doing
an illegal excavation?

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.860
So, you <i>are</i> pirates then!

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:48.250
Recon 01.

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:49.700
This is HQ.

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:52.940
Give priority to capturing the
accused Fujima corporation.

00:20:53.010 --> 00:20:55.840
I repeat, priority to the Fujima corporation.

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:58.490
Recon 01 to HQ.

00:20:58.810 --> 00:21:00.060
Order received.

00:21:00.290 --> 00:21:02.300
Prioritizing Fujima corporation's apprehension.

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:07.330
We're moving away from the military!

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:08.620
Away!

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.610
Great thing we didn't get captured, eh?

00:21:10.610 --> 00:21:12.200
It's not great!

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:15.890
At this point I'll be stuck in
I-machine forever!

00:22:54.650 --> 00:22:55.570
What?

00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:58.130
Did I return?

00:23:04.040 --> 00:23:06.000
My head hurts...

00:23:06.220 --> 00:23:07.420
Where am I?

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:09.180
Aboard Stulti.

00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:12.140
Oh, so that body really was yours, little lady.

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:15.890
Good thing you were able to return
to your body, isn't it, Maya?

00:23:15.890 --> 00:23:16.300
Huh?

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:22.460
How did my body end up on this ship?

00:23:25.940 --> 00:23:28.750
<i>The moment the drill hits the ore,</i>

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:31.180
<i>I notice that my heart skips a beat.</i>

00:23:31.820 --> 00:23:34.520
<i>Will you be able to make it</i>

00:23:34.590 --> 00:23:35.920
<i>or will you die?</i>

00:23:36.550 --> 00:23:39.490
<i>There's no response to this question.</i>

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:39.930
FORMLESS MINERALS
